innova2-app (1.3.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * innova2-smi check: the one DDR write fenced in a warm reboot's link-down
    window is INFO ddr.fenced_linkdown_benign, not WARN ddr.fenced, only when
    the fenced count is <= the link-downs since configuration, the first
    fenced access is a write at 0x200000000 and, on E7 shells, the last
    fenced access lies within 2 s after the last link-down (link-down ->
    recalibration measured 1.12 s). Shells without event timestamps are
    judged on count, address and link-down count, and the evidence says so.
    Anything else stays WARN ddr.fenced (with the reason); route V's
    fenced-while-KEPT stays FAIL. A fence before the last of several
    link-downs (hpy440: two link-downs per warm reboot, the fence in the
    first) cannot be placed from the registers: 'check --recorder' (opt-in,
    stores to the flight-recorder index) requires every FENCE record to lie
    in a LINK_DOWN..RECAL_DONE window.
  * innova2-smi test validate: xbutil's "[PASSED WITH WARNINGS]" (pcie-link
    on an x4 link) counts as passed; the warning text is shown and the PASS
    verdict carries a note instead of dropping the test.

 -- Michal Kouril <xmkouril@gmail.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 07:43:56 -0400

innova2-app (1.3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * innova2-smi status/check: the interface uuid is read passively from
    xocl's (else xclmgmt's) sysfs interface_uuids, else (XRT 2.17 answers
    EINVAL for these shells) from the header of the boot xsabin loaded for the
    card's ROM_TS; the per-build table is only a cross-check and a mismatch is
    a WARN (identity.uuid_mismatch). The
    table now has E7a3-2666ca48 (869cfe84...); every entry re-checked against
    its build's boot.xsabin / bandwidth.xclbin headers and chain.out.
  * status: the throttle line says what is in effect ("in effect: FULL (not
    throttled)"), the FORCE setting on its own line ("FORCE: off (force level
    if enabled: 1/2)") and the automatic tiers ("auto tiers: T1=1/2, T2=1/4").
  * check: UEs are judged against a clean point (configuration or an
    ecc-baseline). After a warm reboot, UEs whose last one follows the last
    link-down are WARN ddr.ue_stale ("likely stale-data reads after warm
    reboot", hint: contents lost in the link-down MIG reset; re-fill, then
    ecc-baseline, or cold boot); where the shell cannot tell stale from fresh
    it says so (WARN ddr.ue_unclassified). UEs with no link-down since the
    clean point stay FAIL.
  * innova2-smi ecc-baseline [--show|--remove]: records CE/UE/link-down counts
    and FPGA uptime per card in ~/.cache/innova2-smi/; check then judges only
    errors since it (a new UE is a FAIL) and shows the totals as INFO.

 -- Michal Kouril <xmkouril@gmail.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 23:43:51 -0400

